---
const stages = [
	{
		title: 'Shop',
		body: 'Consolidated ingredients by supplier, whole-pack buying, and trusted on-hand quantities.'
	},
	{
		title: 'Prep',
		body: 'Scaled dishes, whole sub-recipe batches, instructions, labels, and checkoffs.'
	},
	{
		title: 'Pack',
		body: 'Dishes, quantities, equipment, and completion checks before the order leaves.'
	}
];
---

<section id="operations" class="border-y border-hairline bg-cream" aria-labelledby="operations-heading">
	<div class="container-page py-section">
		<div class="max-w-3xl" data-reveal>
			<h2 id="operations-heading" class="text-h2 font-semibold">Change a draft guest count and the kitchen plan changes with it.</h2>
			<p class="mt-5 max-w-[68ch] text-lede text-ink-soft">
				Choose a menu, enter the event and guest count, and set the selling price. CostCook
				compares theoretical food cost with your target and names the selling price that
				would meet it. Confirm when the plan is ready to freeze.
			</p>
		</div>

		<div class="mt-10 grid items-start gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[4fr_7fr] lg:gap-16">
			<dl class="divide-y divide-ticket-rule border-y border-ticket-rule" data-reveal>
				{
					stages.map((stage) => (
						<div class="py-5">
							<dt class="font-display text-h3 font-semibold">{stage.title}</dt>
							<dd class="mt-2 text-ink-soft">{stage.body}</dd>
						</div>
					))
				}
			</dl>

			<figure data-reveal>
				<picture>
					<source media="(max-width: 639px)" srcset="/proof/shop-mobile.png" />
					<img
						src="/proof/shop.png"
						alt="A CostCook shopping list grouped by supplier, showing each ingredient's need, on-hand amount, whole packs to buy, and supplier subtotal."
						width="1808"
						height="1040"
						loading="lazy"
						decoding="async"
						class="h-auto w-full bg-paper shadow-ticket"
					/>
				</picture>
				<figcaption class="mt-4 text-sm text-ink-soft">
					Trusted shelf quantities reduce buying. They do not reduce the theoretical food the event consumes.
				</figcaption>
			</figure>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
